Custody and asset segregation (FIN-CUS-06)

Issuer: Tatra Wealth, o. c. p., a. s. · IČO 36 012 445 · Hodžovo námestie 3, 811 06 Bratislava

Client financial instruments and client money are held separately from the firm's own assets, in client accounts at an approved custodian, as zákon č. 566/2001 Z. z. requires. The firm never takes physical possession of securities.
Book-entry securities are registered with Centrálny depozitár cenných papierov SR or with the custodian's nominee account, and reconciliation runs daily.
A standing authorisation to move assets to a third party is accepted only in writing, with the destination account named in the mandate.
A change of payment instructions is verified by call-back to a telephone number already on file, never to a number supplied in the same message as the change.
Client asset records are reconciled monthly against the custodian statement, and any break is escalated the same day.
An independent audit of client asset protection is performed annually and its report goes to Národná banka Slovenska.

